---
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import Specimen from '../Specimen.astro';
---
<Specimen title="Variants" surface="alt" code={'<Button href="…" variant="primary">Primary</Button>\n<Button href="…">Secondary</Button>\n<Button href="…" variant="danger">Danger</Button>\n<Button href="…" variant="spectral">Spectral</Button>\n<Button href="…" variant="ghost" trailingIcon="arrow-right-bold">Ghost</Button>'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes">
        <p>Stride's buttons: soft squircle rectangles with a lighter edge on top and a darker one underneath, lifting slightly on hover and pressing in on click.</p>
        <p><strong>Primary</strong> is the monochrome brand (near-black in light, near-white in dark) for the one action that matters most. <strong>Secondary</strong> is Stride's outline button, a raised surface. <strong>Danger</strong> is for destructive actions. <strong>Spectral</strong> is the ONIXLabs addition: a raised button wearing the turning brand gradient, at most once per page. <strong>Ghost</strong> is the content alone, text and icons with no surface, edges or shadow, for a secondary action beside a stronger one.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <div class="cluster">
        <Button href="#variants" variant="primary">Primary</Button>
        <Button href="#variants">Secondary</Button>
        <Button href="#variants" variant="danger">Danger</Button>
        <Button href="#variants" variant="spectral">Spectral</Button>
        <Button href="#variants" variant="ghost" trailingIcon="arrow-right-bold">Ghost</Button>
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="On a dark band" surface="dark">
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>The same buttons inside a near-black band in light mode.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="cluster">
        <Button href="#on-a-dark-band" variant="primary">Primary</Button>
        <Button href="#on-a-dark-band">Secondary</Button>
        <Button href="#on-a-dark-band" variant="danger">Danger</Button>
        <Button href="#on-a-dark-band" variant="spectral">Spectral</Button>
        <Button href="#on-a-dark-band" variant="ghost" trailingIcon="arrow-right-bold">Ghost</Button>
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Sizes" code={'<Button href="…" size="small">Small</Button>\n<Button href="…" size="large">Large</Button>'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Large buttons belong in heroes and the closing call to action, small ones in dense controls; default size everywhere else.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="cluster">
        <Button href="#sizes" variant="primary" size="large">Large</Button>
        <Button href="#sizes" variant="primary">Default</Button>
        <Button href="#sizes" variant="primary" size="small">Small</Button>
        <Button href="#sizes" size="small">Small secondary</Button>
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="With icons" code={'<Button href="…" external>View on GitHub</Button>\n<Button href="…" variant="ghost" trailingIcon="arrow-right-bold">Find out more</Button>'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Buttons carry no leading icon: the label does the work. The one icon is the trailing arrow on a ghost button, which says the action moves on. External links open in a new tab and say so to screen readers.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="cluster">
        <Button href="#with-icons" variant="primary">Send a message</Button>
        <Button href="https://github.com/onix-labs" external>View on GitHub</Button>
        <Button href="#with-icons">Book a meeting</Button>
        <Button href="#with-icons" variant="ghost" trailingIcon="arrow-right-bold">Find out more</Button>
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Pairing">
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>At most one primary and one secondary side by side. A link-style call to action can follow them.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="cluster">
        <Button href="#pairing" variant="primary" size="large">Explore products</Button>
        <Button href="#pairing" size="large">Work with us</Button>
        <Button href="#pairing" variant="link">Read the docs</Button>
    </div>
</Specimen>
